Chapter: C64SidStream
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites C64 chapter Sid
  cites Kernel chapter HdaAudio

 Streams several frames of SID PCM through the HDA output the way an
 emulator's per-frame audio does: one short buffer rendered and played
 each frame, with the oscillators and envelopes carried across frames in
 a persistent state block (sid-render-stream, not the self-contained
 sid-render). A test cannot hear the result, so codex-vm counts every
 buffer it drains to the DAC and exposes the total at HDA #180; this test
 plays a known number of buffers and asserts the count. That proves the
 streaming plumbing -- persistent state, per-frame render, and the
 re-run-each-frame HDA path -- delivers every buffer, independent of
 whether the host has a speaker. The synthesis itself is checked by
 c64-sid; here the point is that successive buffers all flow.

 The registers are left silent on purpose: the drain counter increments
 for every buffer regardless of its contents, so a silent stream proves
 the plumbing without making the battery play a tone. c64-sid-beep is the
 audible one, run by hand.

Section: Body

  frames : Integer = 8
  samples-per-frame : Integer = 768

  play-frame : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Audio] Integer
  play-frame (regbase) (rt) (buf) =
    let r = sid-render-stream regbase rt buf samples-per-frame
    in hda-play-pcm buf (samples-per-frame * 4)

  stream-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Audio] Integer
  stream-loop (regbase) (rt) (buf) (i) =
    if i >= frames then 0
    else act
      p <- play-frame regbase rt buf
      rest <- stream-loop regbase rt buf (i + 1)
      p + rest
    end

  opening : [Console, Audio, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    let regs = alloc-bytes 32
    in let rt = alloc-bytes 64
    in let z = sid-rt-reset rt
    in let buf = alloc-bytes (samples-per-frame * 4)
    in act
      played <- stream-loop regs rt buf 0
      count <- hda-drained-count
      if count == frames then print-line-uni "PASS"
      else print-line-uni ("FAIL: drained " & show count)
    end
  end
